  "characteristics": {
    "kind": "Multivariate run-to-failure time series under real flight conditions",
    "feature_dimensions": {
      "summary": "14 measured sensors + 4 flight-condition inputs; optional 14 virtual sensors and 10 health-modifier channels",
      "counting": "Default loaders expose unit, cycle, flight class, health state, four W_* flight conditions, and 14 X_s sensors. Virtual sensors (X_v) and health modifiers (T) are opt-in. Per-cycle RUL is provided in Y_*.",
      "sources": [
        {
          "name": "Chao et al., Data 2021",
          "url": "https://doi.org/10.3390/data6010005"
        },
        {
          "name": "NASA / PHM Society mirror",
          "url": "https://phm-datasets.s3.amazonaws.com/NASA/17.+Turbofan+Engine+Degradation+Simulation+Data+Set+2.zip"
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  "tasks": [
    "RUL estimation",
    "Prognostics",
    "Fault diagnostics"
  ],
  "task_support": {
    "anomaly_detection": "derived",
    "fault_classification": "derived",
    "condition_estimation": "derived",
    "rul_prediction": "direct",
    "time_to_event": "direct",
    "survival_analysis": "direct"
  },
  "attributes": [
    {
      "name": "unit_number",
      "dtype": "UInt16",
      "role": "entity",
      "description": "Engine unit identifier within the selected subset."
    },
    {
      "name": "cycle",
      "dtype": "UInt32",
      "role": "time",
      "description": "Flight/cycle index along the run-to-failure trajectory."
    },
    {
      "name": "Fc",
      "dtype": "Float64",
      "role": "operating-condition",
      "description": "Flight-class label from the auxiliary table."
    },
    {
      "name": "hs",
      "dtype": "Float64",
      "role": "asset-attribute",
      "description": "Health-state indicator from the auxiliary table."
    },
    {
      "name": "alt, Mach, TRA, T2",
      "dtype": "Float64",
      "role": "operating-condition",
      "description": "Flight-condition / scenario descriptors (W_*)."
    },
    {
      "name": "T24..Wf",
      "dtype": "Float64",
      "role": "sensor",
      "description": "Fourteen measured sensor channels (X_s_*)."
    },
    {
      "name": "RUL",
      "dtype": "Int64",
      "role": "target",
      "description": "Per-cycle remaining useful life from Y_dev / Y_test."
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "The official NASA distribution is a ~15.7 GB nested ZIP. PdMData downloads one HDF5 subset at a time through a Kaggle mirror of the same files (default: ds01).",
    "Each subset file contains development (dev) and test splits with aligned A/W/X_s/X_v/T/Y tables.",
    "DS01 is the smallest practical subset for smoke tests (~2.9 GB, 6 development units and 4 test units).",
    "Unit IDs are local to each subset file; do not join units across variants.",
    "Cite Chao, Kulkarni, Goebel, and Fink (2021) when using this dataset."
  ],
  "citation": "M. Chao, C. Kulkarni, K. Goebel and O. Fink (2021). Aircraft Engine Run-to-Failure Dataset under Real Flight Conditions. NASA Prognostics Data Repository, NASA Ames Research Center."
}
